  3170	    // We want to compress position-independent executable (gcc -pie)
  3171	    // main programs, but compressing a shared library must be avoided
  3172	    // because the result is no longer usable.  In theory, there is no way
  3173	    // to tell them apart: both are just ET_DYN.  Also in theory,
  3174	    // neither the presence nor the absence of any particular symbol name
  3175	    // can be used to tell them apart; there are counterexamples.
  3176	    // However, we will use the following heuristic suggested by
  3177	    // Peter S. Mazinger <ps.m@gmx.net> September 2005:
  3178	    // If a ET_DYN has __libc_start_main as a global undefined symbol,
  3179	    // then the file is a position-independent executable main program
  3180	    // (that depends on libc.so.6) and is eligible to be compressed.
  3181	    // Otherwise (no __libc_start_main as global undefined): skip it.
  3182	    // Also allow  __uClibc_main  and  __uClibc_start_main .
  3183	
